Subject: media: ipu6: ipu7: write ISYS frames through the snooped path

The IPU7 ISYS output pin is cleared and never sets link.is_snoop, so the
IPU writes captured frames without snooping the CPU caches. Userspace
reads capture buffers through cached mappings (libcamera's software ISP,
CPU and GPU upload paths alike), and on x86 dma_sync_*_for_cpu() does
not invalidate, so cache lines still holding a buffer's previous frame
are read back as stale data: 32-pixel, one-row runs of old pixels that
show up as orange and blue dashes along moving edges (Surface Pro 12
Intel, IPU 7.5, OV13858 and IMX681, 1920x1080 through libcamera).

Set is_snoop for the output pin. The IPU7 MMU configurations already
include an IS_DATA_WR_SNOOP stream. With it the dashes are gone on both
cameras at unchanged frame rate (tested on the staging ipu7 driver, which
had the same is_snoop = 0).
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu7-fw-isys.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu7-fw-isys.c
index b1211e24562d..b0d00907d7c6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu7-fw-isys.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu7-fw-isys.c
@@ -214,6 +214,12 @@ static int ipu7_isys_fw_pin_cfg(struct ipu6_isys_video *av,
 	output_pin->link.pbk_slot_id = IPU7_MSG_LINK_PBK_SLOT_ID_DONT_CARE;
 	output_pin->link.dest = 0; /* IPU_INSYS_OUTPUT_LINK_DEST_MEM */
 	output_pin->link.use_sw_managed = 1;
+	/*
+	 * Write frames through the snooped path: the CPU reads capture
+	 * buffers through cached mappings, and non-snooped writes leave
+	 * stale lines of the buffer's previous frame in the CPU cache.
+	 */
+	output_pin->link.is_snoop = 1;
 	output_pin->crop.line_top = 0;
 	output_pin->crop.line_bottom = 0;
 	output_pin->dpcm.enable = 0;
